      "updated": 1767032138106,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "provide categories\nfor a tweet_id\ntweet_id -> []categories",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "provide categories\nfor a tweet_id\ntweet_id -> []categories",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "G-IZblfQvMo9OqCwEZt_u",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1716.9908703096385,
      "y": 827.2326374905739,
      "width": 714.53955078125,
      "height": 750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "ap",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1116151587,
      "version": 1086,
      "versionNonce": 1503479683,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1767036465351,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "per category (consumer)\nbatch wirtes (100 writes or 100ms)\n\nfor hot categories, we can partiton further by\nsecondary id (hash(hashtag))\n\nmaintain sorted set for 1 min window\ncategory_key -> f(category, ?<shard> ,event ts)\nvalue -> sorted set(hash_tag, count)\n\nfor each event\nZINCRBY category_key 1 hashtag (increment count per key)\nZREMRANGEBYRANK key 0 -1501 (enforces max size of the sorted set)\n\n\nexpire the 1 min widow in 65 min (max window + grace period)\n\nconsiderations:\n1. maintain watermark timestamp per category shard\nto drop late coming events below the \nwatermark\n\n2. if the category processors crash, they can resume from the\n    last commited offset\n3. we can maintain high availability for for redis servers by using\n    redis sentinel\n4. rolloup cron can perform periodic snapshots to S3\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "per category (consumer)\nbatch wirtes (100 writes or 100ms)\n\nfor hot categories, we can partiton further by\nsecondary id (hash(hashtag))\n\nmaintain sorted set for 1 min window\ncategory_key -> f(category, ?<shard> ,event ts)\nvalue -> sorted set(hash_tag, count)\n\nfor each event\nZINCRBY category_key 1 hashtag (increment count per key)\nZREMRANGEBYRANK key 0 -1501 (enforces max size of the sorted set)\n\n\nexpire the 1 min widow in 65 min (max window + grace period)\n\nconsiderations:\n1. maintain watermark timestamp per category shard\nto drop late coming events below the \nwatermark\n\n2. if the category processors crash, they can resume from the\n    last commited offset\n3. we can maintain high availability for for redis servers by using\n    redis sentinel\n4. rolloup cron can perform periodic snapshots to S3\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
